commit 90ebe9b11393a3940c68a007a5e234b485a59704
Author: fangyibo <fangyibo@xiaomi.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 17 11:10:07 2026 +0800

    drivers/usbhost: fix UVC alt fallback, buffer race and cleanup path

    VELAPLATFO-94706

    Three independent defects in the UVC class driver, found while bringing
    it up on a host whose isochronous transfers are driven through a vendor
    stream API.  None of them is required to make a camera stream, and none
    was observed to trigger on the hardware used here, but all three are
    reachable.

    Alternate setting fallback:

      uvc_set_interface_alt() falls back to the alternate setting with the
      largest payload when none of them can carry the negotiated
      dwMaxPayloadTransferSize.  The loop recorded the payload but not the
      alternate setting it belongs to, so SET_INTERFACE was issued for the
      initial value of desired_alt, which is 1.  Record the setting together
      with the payload, and report both: reaching this path at all means the
      descriptors and the negotiated payload disagree.

    Capture buffer pointer:

      buffer_addr and buffer_size are written by the application thread
      through IMGDATA_SET_BUF and read by the thread that assembles frames,
      which then copies a whole frame to that address.  There was no
      synchronisation between the two, so a torn read could pair a stale
      address with a new size and overrun the buffer.  Protect the pair with
      a spinlock and take a snapshot of it before use.

    Cleanup worker:

      uvc_device_cleanup_worker() built the device path from
      priv->dev->minor.  capture_unregister() may free dev while priv
      outlives it, so read the minor from priv instead.

    Change-Id: I134adadfed92a61a5823273eddaa89aff8e7341b
    Signed-off-by: fangyibo <fangyibo@xiaomi.com>

