    drivers/usbhost: fix UVC capture thread join and stream restart

    VELAPLATFO-94706

    Two independent defects prevented the UVC capture pipeline from being
    torn down and then restarted.

    uvc_imgdata_stop_capture() joined the capture thread with waitpid(),
    which can never complete for a thread created by kthread_create().
    group_allocate() puts every kernel thread into the single shared
    g_kthread_group, so when the capture thread exits the
    sq_is_singular(&chgrp->tg_members) test in nxtask_sigchild() still sees
    the other kernel threads and skips both nxtask_groupexit() and
    group_signal().  CHILD_FLAG_EXITED is therefore never set and SIGCHLD is
    never delivered, and the caller stays blocked in nxsig_waitinfo() even
    though the thread has already returned.  nxtask_save_parent() does
    allocate a child status entry for the kernel thread, so the parentage
    checks in nxsched_waitpid() pass and the call really does reach the wait
    instead of failing with ECHILD.  Join on a semaphore that the capture
    thread posts as its last action instead, and claim the teardown with
    atomic_xchg() so that only one of uvc_imgdata_uninit() and the
    disconnect work queue can consume that single post.

    uvc_imgdata_start_capture() ran the probe/commit and SET_INTERFACE
    sequence only when the requested format differed from
    current_format_idx and current_frame_idx.  uvc_imgsensor_stop_capture()
    returns the interface to alternate setting 0 but leaves those cached
    indices untouched, so restarting the stream with the same format skipped
    the sequence, the device stayed on the zero bandwidth setting and no
    isochronous data arrived.  Run the sequence whenever the device is not
    on a streaming alternate setting.

    The capture thread also resubmitted slots from the middle of its
    completion scan after thread_running had been cleared, because that flag
    is only evaluated at the top of the loop.  Such a late resubmit reaches
    the host controller while it is stopping the stream and fails.  Check
    the flag again before resubmitting.

    Change-Id: I4b3d1bbf53105ac3640ff8e09484572c263b57dd
    Signed-off-by: fangyibo <fangyibo@xiaomi.com>

