**Purpose**: A binary semaphore used to **join** (wait for exit of) the capture thread, replacing the broken `waitpid()`.

**Why waitpid didn't work**: The commit message explains — for `kthread_create()` threads, `waitpid()` never completes because all kernel threads share `g_kthread_group`, so `nxtask_sigchild()` skips setting `CHILD_FLAG_EXITED`/delivering SIGCHLD (the `sq_is_singular(&chgrp->tg_members)` test still sees other kernel threads). So `waitpid` blocks forever even after the thread returns.

